s but because you have spent  the last three movies basically  distancing yourself and being more  realistic and grounded about it if  you're gonna introduce these new  elements you have to justify them you  can't just throw them in because that's  just what bond does the way that you  could in the classic era because back  then that is just what bond was but  that's not the case now and even when I  think back to the bond era it was  usually at least a lip service to  explain why these things were in there  even though the real answer was because  it's a bond trope like Blofeld's base in  the middle of nowhere in that crater I I  don't know why it's there  I mean it's not a lab where he's dealing  with some materials that he has to keep  away from society there's nothing about  that location that has something like  right there geographically that he has  to be set up there as far as what's he's  doing it's basically it's a surveillance  farm pretty much I mean they think I set  that up in an abandoned parking  structure there's just no reason given  it's just here's the villains base in  the middle of nowhere but like I said  classic are they at least gave us a  reason like it may be stupid but I know  why Drax has a space station and  Moonraker I know why Alec Trevelyan has  buried a satellite dish underneath a  lake in gold and I same thing with the  torture scene for bond he strapped to a  chair and tortured why I honestly I  don't know aside from it's a trope they  wanted to reinsert because Blofeld's not  trying to get information from it he's  making Madeleine Swann watch but he's  not trying to get her to crack either he  doesn't even seem to be enjoying it so  it's not like he's torturing him for fun  he's just kind of doing it which of  course does bring us to blow fell which  is kind of the big thing here and in  most ways he's the big thing that  doesn't work because first of all we  have to talk about the fact that it's  it's like a twist or revealed that this  is even Blofeld in the first place which  was just really stupid I honestly did  not believe this guy was gonna turn out  to be Blofeld not because I didn't see  the indicators that we all saw but  because they were saying this is not  Blofeld and I actually thought they  can't be so stupid as to try and pull  that trick off because what's the  immediate comparison you think of you  think of the reveal of Khan in Star Trek  into darkness now just to be clear me  personally I didn't have the big problem  with the Khan revealed that I know a lot  of people did although I understand why  people were upset by that I kind of  rolled with it but it becomes that sort  of fool me once shame on me fool me  twice shame on you things so the fact  that this movie only a few years after  star trek into darkness do it and  arguably that movie didn't even get away  with it that well you're gonna do it  again that just shows contempt for the  audience cuz yeah we were all going come  on Christoph vols he's blow fell doesn't  he and they were like no  he's not Blofeld no no no no no  definitely not blow fell but come on you  brought back Specter if you're bringing  back Specter why wouldn't you bring back  both he can just admit to us that he's  booked no he's not Blofeld no no no and  then you get to the movies like and he's  Blofeld ha we got you know you didn't  get us you lied to us and we didn't even  believe you it's like that gag from  Family Guy where Chris goes up to Megan  goes hey Meg guess what I'm thinking  it's not kidding I don't know Chris what  are you thinking it was Kitty hahahaha  that's what it feels like the movie is  doing and frankly it's insulting and the  fact that we are in a rebooted  continuity him revealing himself to be  Blofeld has no meaning we just have him  show up and be Blofeld that's not a  twist unless you are a fan of old bond  and all the fans of old bond already  called that so if they just had a  blood-filled for the from the get-go  that would have helped it wouldn't have  fixed the whole problem though because  we got the second part of why Blofeld  doesn't work which is this revealed that  he's James Bond's brother kinda sorta  foster brother stepbrother whatever how  is that relevant how does that give us  anything because we're shown nothing  about their relationship about their  history about their past we have no idea  what their life together was like I mean  there's a tiny bit of a hint from  Blofeld that he resented bond for coming  into his life but we don't know if that  was evident to bomb when they were kids  were they friends when they were kids we  didn't did they were they at least  cordial just bond feel betrayed by the  fact that this guy was kind of his  brother he doesn't seem to feel betrayed  actually he doesn't seem surprised at  all so what about their relationship  with our younger makes him not surprised  by this I don't know the answer any of  that because the movie doesn't show us  the only thing that I can think of as to  why they might have done this might have  been to try and offset the fact that the  stakes overall are a bit weak because  spectres big plant is just basically to  consolidate the world's major  surveillance and then take control of  that now while I'll grant that is a bad  thing I understand why that's something  we don't want to have happen that's  pretty low stakes in James Bond's world  you know no one's going to die as an  immediate result of this nothing's  blowing up there's no death laser it's  just they can watch everything okay  that's bad I guess so I feel like they  tried to pull off what goldeneye pulled  off because golden i also had lower  stakes cuz then that one Trevelyan was  going to electronically steal money and  then basically use EMP to shut down all  the electronics in London which again a  bad thing that probably would have been  a couple of immediate that's from that  but ultimately it's just a blackout and  London could have recovered from that  but the way they offset the low stakes  was by raising the personal stakes  because the history between Trevelyan  and bond but in that movie they showed  us that history and they showed us the  sense of betrayal that bond had towards  him and they don't show us that here so  if that was what they were trying to do  by introducing this history they botched  it completely and if that's not what  they were trying to do then what were  they trying to do I would have bought  the motivation so much better for  Blofeld if he just said look I had these  plans going on and over the course of  the last three movies you kept stumbling  into and screwing up my plan so I'm  pissed at you and I'm gonna torture you  now I want to roll with that that was  that would have been fine but this this  whole notion that they've got history  and they grew up together with why what  does that what purpose does that serve  look I want to be clear again the first  hour of this thing is phenomenal and  honestly in the second half it's not all  bad either there are some good points  the fight on the train is terrific we've  got some good moments like that but the  thing is the film as a whole it started  good it got great and then it hit that  point where it started to dip down and  then the good stuff that's in the latter  have it just sort of evens out for a  minute before continuing to dive  downwards I was frustrated when I left  the theater and as I have thought about  it since then it's just made me angry  and I just have a hard time believing  that the first half of this film which  is so brilliant and perfectly executed  in these classic bond elements  wonderfully integrated and the second  half of this film where it's just a  going through a check  list of tropes were made by the same  people this is probably the Bond film I  am most frustrated with it disappointed  by it's not the worst Bond film it's not  even the worst Daniel Craig Bond film  that's easily still quantum of solace  but it is definitely the biggest  disappointment I've ever had watching  bond so that's it for me have you seen  Specter if you have what did you think  about it whatever you thought drop  something down in the comments and let's  talk about it until next time this  council is adjourned
 

